title: Start
---

Rain taps softly against the window.
A cramped studio apartment. Bills scattered across a small table. The room is dim except for the light of a phone screen.
Alice stares at the screen. 
//<<play_animation Player Black>>

Alice: …Rent… electricity… overdue notice?

Alice exhales.

Alice: I can’t keep stretching it like this.

Her stomach growls. 

Alice: …I really need a job. Anything at this point.

She goes to job search site and scrolls through job listings.

Part-time Café Staff – Experience required
Convenience Store Night Shift – Minimum wage
Warehouse Sorting – Heavy lifting required

Alice: Minimum wage… heavy lifting… I won’t survive on that.

She scrolls further down.
The scrolling slows.

Private Residence | High Pay – Paid Immediately After Completion, No Experience Required

Alice: ... One week?

She taps the listing.

- Clean designated areas only
- Do not enter restricted rooms
- Follow all instructions strictly
- Live-out position
- Generous compensation
A phone number is listed below. No company name. No address.

Alice: ... Private residence?

She frowns.

Alice: No company name… no photos… no reviews…

She scrolls. Nothing more.

Alice: That's suspicious. But...

She breathes in.

Alice: The pay. 

She rereads the number.

Alice: That’s more than I'd make in a month.

The rain outside grows slightly louder.

What should I do?

-> Ignore it.
    Alice: It’s probably some scam.
    Alice: ... Or even worse. 
    A small pause.
    Alice: ... But what if it isn't?
    She glances back at the unpaid bills.
    Alice: I just need one week.
    <<jump PhoneCall>>
-> Call now.
    <<jump PhoneCall>>

===
title: PhoneCall
---
//<<play_animation Player Grey>>

The phone rings once. 
Twice.

Click.

???: Hello?

Her voice is steady. Almost too steady.

Alice: Ah, he- hello. I'm calling you about the cleaning job...

A brief pause.

???: A-ha. You saw the listing. 

Alice: Yes... 

???: Can you come tomorrow right away? 8:00 PM.

Alice: Tomorrow evening? Ah, yes! I can do that.

???: Good. I need someone who follows directions and works without causing any trouble. Do you understand?

Alice: Y-yes, of course. I won't cause any trouble.

???: The address is 104 Blackwood Lane. Don't be late.

Click.

Alice: ...Hello? She hung up.

Alice: 104 Blackwood Lane... Am I really going to be okay with this job?

Alice: ...I should look around my room and then get some sleep for tomorrow.

<<set $has_finished_phone_call = true>>
===

title: Mansion_Entrance_Arrival
---
Alice: So this is the house... 

Alice: It's much bigger and darker than I imagined.

Alice: Well, no turning back now... Let's go knock on the door.
===

title: First_Talk
---

Before you try to knock on the door, the door opens by itself.

<<move_butler LivingRoom>>
<<teleport_with_delay LivingRoom_Transition 2.0>>

Alice: ...! He-Hello.

Butler: You arrived just on time. Come on in.

Butler: This is our living room.
Butler: If you follow the red carpet upstairs, the first door you see on the second floor will be where you'll be working.

Alice: Ah... yes!
Alice: 'Wow, getting straight to business as soon as I arrive...'

<<teleport_with_delay Bedroom_Transition 1.0>>
<<move_butler Bedroom>>

Butler: This is your room. Rest today, and your work will start tomorrow.
Butler: And wear these while you stay here.

*butler turns around to alice, hands the uniform*

Butler: ... You are free to do as you like, but there is one thing I must ask you not to do.
Butler: Do not pry around trying to find out too much.

Butler: As for today, feel free to rest and look around the mansion. Just make sure not to cause any trouble.
Butler: I will see you tomorrow morning.

Alice: Ah, thank...

// 3. 화면 페이드아웃되는 동안 집사를 복도로 이동시킴
<<fade_screen_sleep>>
<<move_butler Hallway>>

Alice: ... She just left. 

Alice: Wow... the room's really old and small.
Alice: Well, at least it has a bed...
Alice: Before I look around the mansion, I should change into the maid uniform first.

<<change_clothes Maid>>

Alice: Alright, everything fits. Time to explore.

===

title: Normal_Ending
---
(The sun rises on Day {$day_count}. You've completed your 3 days of work at the mansion...)

Alice: My time here is done. Let's get changed first...

<<change_clothes Modern>>
===

title: Normal_Ending_Cutscene
---
// This runs as soon as Alice steps on the trigger box outside the Bedroom on Day4
Alice: !
Butler: Good morning.
Alice: Ah, good mor-
Butler: You have done a great job for last three days.
Butler: Money is sent through your bank accound this morning.
Alice: Oh, thank... thank you. 
Alice: 'That was very quick...'
Butler: You may leave as soon as you pack up.
-> Alice: Can I say good byes to other people before I leave?
    Butler: No, I need you to leave ASAP. 
    Alice: 'She's in such a hurry...'
    Alice: O, okay.
    Butler: I'll walk you to the door. 
-> Alice: I think I'm ready to leave.
    Butler: Great. I'll walk you to the door. 

<<teleport_with_delay Exit_Transition 1.5>>

Alice: ...
Alice: That felt like a dream...
Alice: ...
Alice: ......
Alice: Let's go home. 

<<jump Normal_Ending_Monologue>>
===

title: Normal_Ending_Monologue
---
<<fade_screen_sleep>>

(The three days spent at the mansion felt like a strange, fleeting dream.)

(Returning to my cramped studio apartment, I checked my account—the promised payment was already there, exactly down to the last cent.)

(I paid off the overdue bills, the rent, and the utilities that had been weighing on my shoulders for months.)

(Life went right back to normal, as if nothing had ever happened...)

(As if that eerie, quiet mansion was nothing more than a illusion.)

<<jump Normal_Ending_Credit>>
===

title: Normal_Ending_Credit
---

Normal Ending Finished.
===